WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:14.920
Knowledge is power! The more you know,
 the better informed your decision can be.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:22.800
Libraries in that respect play an
incredibly important role in our democracy.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:31.460
The New York Public Library for instance has an amazing collection of Arctic materials.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:37.100
Materials about explorers who went to the Arctic;
lost their lives there.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:44.040
An extraordinary collection of maps of the Arctic 
- some accurate, some inaccurate.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.680
And I think
libraries in that way bringing together

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:56.130
researchers, scientists, artists,
sociologists, psychologists, people from

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:02.670
all walks of life can have a very
important role in better understanding

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.980
the kind of predicament we find
ourselves in today.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:14.960
With everything that's going on in the world today with
various political struggles we might

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:20.660
encounter having to do with climate
change or climate control, with people

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.300
denying the fact that the world maybe is
warming up,

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:35.640
libraries can in some way be the spokesperson. As an institution they nearly can become the place, the hub,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:42.340
the place where people congregate around
ideas and learn what the data is,

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:50.600
learn what the challenges are and make better and informed decisions of how the world is

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:58.800
changing and make those decisions based
on a better acquaintance with what the

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.840
knowledge of the past is and how the
past will inform the future

